    },
    "body": "This fixes the circular dependency checker in circular-dependencies.py.\r\n\r\nThe script previously assumed a single include layout and only resolved headers relative to the current file. That breaks when sources include headers from multiple directories, which can cause missed circular dependency detection.\r\n\r\nThis patch:\r\n\r\nnormalizes module paths before dependency matching\r\nresolves includes relative to the source file and configured include roots\r\nsupports -I include directories\r\npreserves the existing behavior for header-based module paths such as interfaces/\r\nThis improves the reliability of the developer tooling used to catch circular dependencies without changing Bitcoin Core runtime behavior.\r\n\r\nTests:\r\n\r\npython3 -m py_compile contrib/devtools/circular-dependencies.py\r\npython3 circular-dependencies.py src/*.h src/*.cpp",
